.TH ORO-LAUNCHER 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:launcher \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:launcher'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Android named destinations. Requires `[launcher] enabled = true`. A shortcut produces routing receipts, never authorization or resource mutation. Restore sign\-in and resolve the exact current account/target before opening it.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBgetStatus()\fR
Reads native launcher support without publishing destinations.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBreplace(destinations)\fR
Replaces this runtime's dynamic destinations, preserving unrelated app shortcuts. Removed targets are disabled, including pinned copies. At most 16 entries and Android's per\-activity quota. Must run from a visible window.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdestinations\fR (LauncherDestination[]; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherPublicationResult>\fR
.TP
\fBpin(id)\fR
Requests Android's user\-controlled pin flow for an existing destination. Submission is not confirmation that the user pinned the shortcut.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherPinResult>\fR
.TP
\fBgetResponses()\fR
Reads pending cold/warm launch identities after restoring authorization. Reads do not consume receipts. Validate current IAM and handle removed accounts/targets; opening a shortcut must not replay a mutation.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherReceipt[]>\fR
.TP
\fBacknowledgeResponse(receiptId)\fR
Acknowledges a reconciled or rejected routing receipt. Repeat acknowledgements are allowed. Call only after authenticated target resolution has completed.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIreceiptId\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
